A||||24||FIEROCIOUS||Fiero on a diet!||||12||
Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||02-25-2000||06:41 AM||||Can any body give me some new ideas on how to make my 87 GT lighter! I would like to take weight off the rear mostly. Anything that is not used is already off but you can always find more fat to trim!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000001||Phil||02-25-2000||06:59 AM||||Battery in front?||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-25-2000||08:44 AM||||I put my car on a quick weight loss program!!!  All the heat shields, A/C,  Steering Dampener, I didn't move the battery.. thought about it thoug.. I need all the weight i can get over the drive wheels! Windsheild washer reservoir, breather tubing and blower motor for the engine compartment. I taking off the heat shields i wrapped EVERYTHING in either ceramic header tape or High temp reflective stick tape from Thermo-Tec. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||02-25-2000||09:49 PM||||front/rear splash shields, lexan sunroof, carpet, passenger seat, radio, speakers, console, (not recomended for street use vehicles)door reinforcement beams, front/rear steel bumpers- the "real" bumper under the cover, headlight units, AC compressor and related hardware, spare tire/jack, heater blower motor, window lift motors (add manual windows), cruise master, rear spoiler, gt body kit, big heavy exhaust system.... That is all I can think of right off the top of my head.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||86SE||02-25-2000||09:55 PM||||take out any loose change, drive naked, put bike tires on it........better yet take out the engine to loose a couple hundred pounds!!||||reg||6
Z||000005||1FST2M6||02-25-2000||11:26 PM||||And don't forget the air in the tires... replace it with Helium!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||02-25-2000||11:35 PM||||You guys are nuts, did you know that? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||kidzwheelz||02-26-2000||12:58 AM||||  I've got two words for you.........Tube Chassis!!!!<P><BR>  Thought I was going to say "Get bent", Huh, Boss!||||reg||12
Z||000008||Oreif||02-26-2000||01:04 AM||||The easiest way is to build the IMSA Fiero race car that is detailed in the Pontac Performance Plus magazine the whole car weighs in at 2100 lbs, and is powered by a 3.0L SD4 engine producing 346 Horses! It has a top speed of 165mph! ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pretender||02-26-2000||02:53 AM||||remove the ac. and ac compressor. get rid of the pass. seat. buy lighter more styleish wheels. and kick out the windshield like Bo and Duke luke did in all those re-runs, replace it with some duct-tape and ziplock baggies all hot glued together?..haha.||||reg||1
Z||000010||FIEROCIOUS||02-26-2000||03:56 AM||||I've taken the A/C out all ready I didn't think about the under bumpers (they may stay though) I have taken the plastic absorbers out. I've got race seats, and all the sound deadening and splash guards have been removed. The battery will be up front soon and am going to get aluminum pulleys. No wing. Lexan windows are now fiberglass scoops. The carpet weighs a ton but I like my cars to look nice too! I'm thinking about the Evap and engine hoist brakets. Any ideas on these? <P>Oreif please give me info on the IMSA fiero that is exactly what I'm going for! ||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||02-26-2000||07:57 AM||||I don't recommend this with the Fiero, but in the old days, I've seen them drilling holes at regular intervals in the frame and have heard of acid dipping the body sheet metal to make it thinner. Here is a page on my website with a couple IMSU racing Fieros.<P> <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/imsa" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/imsa</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||1FST2M6||02-27-2000||02:04 AM||||did you get the rest of the A/C components out along with the compressor? Condensor piping etc. the brackets are out of my car... that huge blower in the trunk that need to go.. most of them don't work anymore anyway and they weigh in at over 10lbs (duct work included)||||reg||1
Z||000013||Formula||02-27-2000||03:08 PM||||if you put helium in your tires youd learn a new meaning for "light them up" lol<P>did you already take the spare tire and jack out?<P>I bet tom's headlight mod weighs a lot less then the motor system.<P>you could probably completly remove the trunk, but that might screw with your perfect weight balance.<P>take the sunroof out!!!!! unless its snowing or raining<P>if your car is a fastback then convert it to a notchback and give me the fast back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I wonder if any of those ferrari dashboard rebody things weigh less then the fiero one?<P>and last but not least, cut out the floorboards, this can improve braking too!||||reg||1
Z||000014||FIEROCIOUS||02-28-2000||03:58 PM||||The blower in the trunk blows cool air on the coil and alternator, How important in this? I've thought about this but was hesitant to do it. Didn't they come out with a new heat shield in 88? What is the part number for this? Will it work with sprint headers? <BR>I changed the air cleaner container so that it has snap clips holding the lid down and the triangular center post support is removed for more air flow, I would realy like to get rid of the EVAP canister because one of the snap clips is in the way, has any one removed their charcoal canister? Could you run the line that goes to the gas tank to the fuel fill opening?<BR>Any help is much apreciated!||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||02-28-2000||10:58 PM||||I pulled the Fan out of my trunk... along with all of the duct work with no increse in engine bay temps... I don't think it work any more anyway... as for the EVAP canister.. the one hooked to the A/C can come out but the one attached to the fuel system will make your car run strange.. I tried that and it bucked and choked and acted stupid... not sure if it was Psychlogical or what but it didn't seem to work for me.  I now have the once open connector to the fan connected to a fan cooling my Crane HI6s in the trunk. (4" 12v 97cfm from ACK radio) Looks kind chezy but it works! dropped it surface temps from 150+ to almost ambient (taken with Infrared temp gun, usually used for taking tire temps at the track, can be purchased at Racer Wholesale)||||reg||1
Z||000016||FIEROCIOUS||03-02-2000||07:00 PM||||OK, I removed the fan in the trunk today, how did you all fill in the holes in the trunk? Also has anyone removed heat shields on their Fieros? I've removed the ones that looked trivial, can anyone give me any more ideas? I want this Fiero light! Has anyone removed the heat shields on the motor mount or tie rod ends? <P>List of weight removed:<BR>Air conditioner and all related parts<BR>Rear vent under covers<BR>Heat shield between rear header and muffler<BR>E-brake cables and brakets (Baretta brakes)<BR>Air cleaner resonator box support (just one)<BR>Battery plastic guard<BR>All splash guards<BR>All sound deadener exept on fire wall<BR>Cruise control<BR>Radio and speakers<BR>Seats (Race seats)<BR>Metal posts under front hood near rear<BR>Jack bracket<BR>Inner fender cut (air to brakes on front)<P>If you have done something I have not found please help.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000017||1FST2M6||03-02-2000||08:20 PM||||i've taken EVERY heat shield out of my car.. and as for the "hole" in the trunk DOn't worry about it... it's to high up to catch any water. all the motor lift brackets.. the A/C bracket, e brake handle... seat belts... (replaced with Jamex 4point) upgrade the headlamps to fixed or flush mount ones and discard the motors and the bracketry... windshield washer reservoir and pump...  take the resonator box off! replace it with a piece of 3" aluminum tubng... carpet out of the trunk...  thats all i can think that i've done right now.. i'm sure i'll think of more....<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Gokart||03-04-2000||06:08 AM||||I like having my tool box with me at all times just in case, but it weighs about 50lbs! Having them in there if I have an on-road problem is more important to me than smoking some rice burner, but would I better off trying to find room up front for them versus the trunk?||||reg||5
Z||000019||batboy||03-04-2000||08:29 AM||||I'm with Gokart, but I've narrowed my emergency tools down to a few that will fit into a very small gym bag like pouch. I carry this up front on the spare tire. A cheap set of sockets and rachet, a cheap set of combination wrenches. A few odd screwdrivers, a crescent wrench, vice-grips, micro-adjusting tool (hammer) and a few other odds 'n' ends. I also carry an extra gallon of antifreeze and a couple quarts of oil, for emegencies.<P>For more weight reduction, you could take all the sound deadening material out and remove the carpet pad, that stuff weighs a lot collectively. You could always put the outer part of the carpet back in so it will look better. Ok, I just saw where you said most of the sound insulation was already removed. Remove the cat and replace it with a straight piece of pipe (peace pipe?). If you can get away with that, better check local regulations.||||reg||1
Z||000020||1FST2M6||03-04-2000||12:00 PM||||the only tools i've ever carried are a 3/8 open end and a 7/16 open end.. in the passenger compartment (glove box thing)... thats all i need to pull out my bottle.. no antifreze or oil... As for the cat removal.. when i tried that i lost torque below 4500 nearly 10lbft of it.. i gained upper range hp but not enough to offset the cost of the lost torque...  only about 4-5hp at 5300... hardly worth the trouble. oh I'm running a 2.5" random technology cat. ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Cooter||03-04-2000||09:22 PM||||To fix the trunk holes, get the block off plates from a 4cyl car. All 85 up fieros have the holes for the fan and pipes, but the 4cyl's just have silver plugs in the holes.||||reg||1
Z||000022||FIEROCIOUS||03-05-2000||08:16 PM||||Hey, Cooter thanks I knew there was something to fill the holes! GM hates to make idividual tooling! The cat has been changed to a random tech unit in mine also!<BR>Any other ideas? I'm looking for at least a total of 150 lb off the rear so far I have removed 50 lbs! the battery will net at least 30 lbs. I want 47/53 F/R ratio.||||reg||14
Z||000023||Phil||03-05-2000||08:41 PM||||Have you checked the thread about the 2100 lb buggy  driver incl.?||||reg||1
